    "result_text": "All tests pass (the build compiles the MapStruct mapper and OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` cleanly, so the new fields map through automatically).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented soft-duplicate flagging on `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate (already rejected by `EnsureUniqueIdentity`) but shares an existing owner's **lastName + postcode** with a **different telephone**, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges, each kept to its single responsibility:\n\n- **New pipeline step** `FlagPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 the only new logic. Mirrors the existing `CountNamesakes`/`AssignHouseholdId` pattern: mutates the built `Owner` in place, scanning `findAll()` (which, running before `SaveOwner`, sees only pre-existing owners). Sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`, reusing `TelephoneNormalizer.toE164` for the telephone comparison rather than duplicating normalization.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the step in between `flagBulkSignup` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 two persisted columns (`possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`) with getters/setters, alongside the other derived fields.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared both as read-only derived fields on the `Owner` schema; MapStruct maps them by name into `OwnerDto`, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns them.\n- **schema.sql** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the two columns to the `owners` table so the `ddl-auto=none` test profile (hsqldb) has them.\n\nThe dedicated `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the full suite are green.",
